  "worked_solution": "Notice that the $4$th column contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $4$th column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(K) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\,-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $3$rd column of the $3\\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(K) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(2-0) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
